# Optimizer state facade — SGD optimizer state (PML4-U3).
#
# Public import: importa ex "gradus:optimize" privata optimize
# Depends on: gradus:dtype (finita), gradus:gradient (Gradiente + obsoletus,
# the U2 gradient-call contract), gradus:parameter (Parametrum + muta, the
# PML1-U5 parameter contract), gradus:tensor (value carrier).
#
# Architectural rule: optimizers consume raw parameter tensors and gradient
# tensors. They do not know about layer abstractions or architectures. This
# module must not import from gradus:nn, gradus:attention, or
# gradus:transformer. No module owns a backend or device handle.
#
# PML0-U3 ledger disposition (pml0-proof-api-ledger.md, gradus 33df687) —
# executed at PML1-U6: RETIRE sgd_step_2x2 (row 10) and sgd_step_4x4 (row
# 11). The retired symbols' update math (param − lr·grad) is inlined in the
# caller-backed steppers train_step_2x2 / train_step_4x4 (src/train.fab,
# rows 16-17, admitted). PML4-U3 restores an optimizer surface ON TOP of
# the PML1 parameter contract (identity) and the U2 gradient-call contract
# (per-parameter gradients with generation) — the retired steppers are not
# revived; the production state contract below is the new surface.
#
# =========================================================================
# The optimizer-state contract (pml4-delivery.md PML4-U3)
# =========================================================================
#
# --- One per-parameter state slot ---------------------------------------
# SGD (first admitted row; batch optimizers after the first accepted —
# campaign batch-by-default). Every trainable parameter owns one state
# slot:
#
#   SgdStatum = identity (possessor + nomen, PML1-U5) + version +
#               generation + step count + learning rate
#
#   versio    — STATE version: mutation counter. Starts at 1; every
#               successful step (passus) bumps it by 1. Identity fields
#               (possessor/nomen) are stable across steps.
#   generatio — the parameter versio at the last applied step (the U2
#               generation seam). A gradient computed at a parameter
#               versio ≠ the parameter's current versio is STALE
#               (gradient.obsoletus) and is rejected before the step.
#   passus    — applied step count for this parameter.
#   lentus    — the learning rate (per-parameter; round-trips exactly in
#               the checkpoint).
#
# --- State mutation rules (explicit) ------------------------------------
# A step (passus) is the only mutation. Preconditions, fail closed with
# the typed OptimizeError:
#   * state identity ≡ parameter identity (IdentitasMismatch);
#   * gradient identity ≡ parameter identity (IdentitasMismatch);
#   * gradient fresh: NOT gradient.obsoletus(g, p.versio()) — the gradient
#     was computed against the parameter's current versio (GradusObsoletus);
#   * parameter trainable — frozen parameters never step (Gelida);
#   * gradient shape ≡ parameter shape (FormaMismatch).
# The update is the accepted SGD row (the retired sgd_step math, the
# train_step_2x2/4x4 formula, the GPU-training lane's per-step update):
#   param' = param − lentus·grad
# via parameter.muta (values-only, bumps the parameter versio by 1). A
# successful step produces the new parameter (versio bumped) and the new
# state slot: versio +1, generatio = the new parameter versio, passus +1.
# State identity and lentus are stable across steps.
#
# --- Serialization (versioned wire, exact round-trip) -------------------
#   slot wire:  "optimizer/sgd-state/1.0.0/<possessor>/<nomen>/<versio>/
#               <generatio>/<passus>/<lentus>"
#   full wire:  "optimizer/sgd/1.0.0/<count>;<slot>;...;<slot>"  (';' = slot
#               separator; empty optimizer has count 0 and no slots)
# The wire reserves '/' (slot field separator) and ';' (slot separator) in
# optimizer identity — an extension of the U5 wire-safety rule ("/"
# reserved) for this module's multi-slot wire, documented and fail-closed.
# The learning rate rides the lossless float-token form (the U7 serialize
# contract's shortest-round-trip textus tokens). A reader rejects unknown
# markers/schema versions, malformed fields, and out-of-range counters —
# fail closed, no best-effort partial reads (capsule rule).
# Checkpoint round-trip predicate: deserializa(serializa(x)) ≡ x by
# statum_aequus / sgd_aequus (field-wise, exact — including the lr).
#
# --- Shared with the GPU-training lane's accepted facts -----------------
#   * update formula param' = param − lr·grad — the retired sgd_step math
#     (pml0-proof-api-ledger.md rows 10-11), the admitted train_step_2x2/
#     4x4 surface (rows 16-17), and the stage-6 per-step update route
#     ("8-step inline SGD lr=0.01"; per-step parameter-update states in the
#     exit gate).
#   * per-parameter identity = (possessor, nomen, versio) — parameter.fab
#     schema_versio 1.0.0 (PML1-U5), the same schema the U2 Gradiente
#     record carries.
#   * gradient freshness composes with the U2 generation seam
#     (gradient.obsoletus).
#
# --- Evidence honesty (CTO Q2, hard) ------------------------------------
# This surface is the STRUCTURAL proof: the state contract (identity,
# version, generation, step-count, mutation rules) and the wire round-trip
# are compile-validated and proven by the co-located proba. Executed VALUE
# identity (the numeric outcome of a step, an exact checkpoint value) is
# env-blocked tree-wide today (FMIR stepper / library-import gap —
# recorded residual). PML4-U3 is PARTIAL: step-value identity is deferred
# to a runtime-evidence gate (auditor-owned faber test path; oracle pins
# recorded in optimize.proba).
importa ex "gradus:dtype" privata dtype
importa ex "gradus:gradient" privata gradient
importa ex "gradus:parameter" privata parametrum
importa ex "gradus:tensor" privata tensor

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Schema constant — any change to the wire layout is a schema bump;
# consumers reject unknown schema versions.
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------

fixum textus schema_versio ← "1.0.0"

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OptimizeError — typed error vocabulary of the optimizer-state contract.
# Every variant carries a textus causa (render via causa).
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------

discretio OptimizeError {
    NomenInane { textus causa },
    VersioInvalida { textus causa },
    GeneratioInvalida { textus causa },
    PassusInvalida { textus causa },
    LentusInvalida { textus causa },
    IdentitasMismatch { textus causa },
    GradusObsoletus { textus causa },
    Gelida { textus causa },
    FormaMismatch { textus causa },
    Mutatio { textus causa },
    NomenDuplicatum { textus causa },
    NomenIgnotum { textus causa },
    VersioIgnota { textus causa },
    WireMala { textus causa }
}

functio causa(OptimizeError e) → textus {
    discerne e {
        casu NomenInane fixum causa { redde causa }
        casu VersioInvalida fixum causa { redde causa }
        casu GeneratioInvalida fixum causa { redde causa }
        casu PassusInvalida fixum causa { redde causa }
        casu LentusInvalida fixum causa { redde causa }
        casu IdentitasMismatch fixum causa { redde causa }
        casu GradusObsoletus fixum causa { redde causa }
        casu Gelida fixum causa { redde causa }
        casu FormaMismatch fixum causa { redde causa }
        casu Mutatio fixum causa { redde causa }
        casu NomenDuplicatum fixum causa { redde causa }
        casu NomenIgnotum fixum causa { redde causa }
        casu VersioIgnota fixum causa { redde causa }
        casu WireMala fixum causa { redde causa }
    }
}

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Wire-safety and numeric-field helpers (the parameter.fab U5 pattern,
# extended: '/' AND ';' are reserved in optimizer identity — the slot and
# slot-separator markers of this module's wire).
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ privata
functio _habeat_solidum(textus s) → bivalens {
    varia numerus i ← 0
    dum i < s.longitudo() {
        si s.accipe(i) ≡ "/" aut s.accipe(i) ≡ ";" ergo redde verum
        i ← i + 1
    }
    redde falsum
}

@ privata
functio _digitum(textus c) → bivalens {
    redde c ≡ "0" aut c ≡ "1" aut c ≡ "2" aut c ≡ "3" aut c ≡ "4" aut c ≡ "5" aut c ≡ "6" aut c ≡ "7" aut c ≡ "8" aut c ≡ "9"
}

@ privata
functio _numerica(textus s) → bivalens {
    si s.longitudo() ≡ 0 ergo redde falsum
    si s.longitudo() > 18 ergo redde falsum
    varia numerus i ← 0
    dum i < s.longitudo() {
        si non (_digitum(s.accipe(i))) ergo redde falsum
        i ← i + 1
    }
    redde verum
}

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SgdStatum — one parameter's SGD state slot: identity + version +
# generation + step count + learning rate. See the header contract.
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------

genus SgdStatum {
    textus possessor
    textus nomen
    numerus versio
    numerus generatio
    numerus passus
    f32 lentus

    # Owner path (identity, PML1-U5).
    functio possessor() → textus {
        redde ego.possessor
    }

    # Parameter name (identity).
    functio nomen() → textus {
        redde ego.nomen
    }

    # State version (mutation counter; starts at 1, bumps per step).
    functio versio() → numerus {
        redde ego.versio
    }

    # Generation: the parameter versio at the last applied step (U2 seam).
    functio generatio() → numerus {
        redde ego.generatio
    }

    # Applied step count.
    functio passus() → numerus {
        redde ego.passus
    }

    # Learning rate (per-parameter; exact in the checkpoint).
    functio lentus() → f32 {
        redde ego.lentus
    }
}

# Field-wise state equality — the checkpoint round-trip predicate
# (deserializa(serializa(x)) ≡ x), exact including the learning rate.
functio statum_aequus(SgdStatum a, SgdStatum b) → bivalens {
    si a.possessor() ≠ b.possessor() ergo redde falsum
    si a.nomen() ≠ b.nomen() ergo redde falsum
    si a.versio() ≠ b.versio() ergo redde falsum
    si a.generatio() ≠ b.generatio() ergo redde falsum
    si a.passus() ≠ b.passus() ergo redde falsum
    si a.lentus() ≠ b.lentus() ergo redde falsum
    redde verum
}

# Shared construction with full validation (used by the public constructor
# and by deserialization — both enter the same fail-closed rules).
@ privata
functio _structum(textus nomen, textus possessor, numerus versio, numerus generatio, numerus passus, f32 lentus) → SgdStatum ⇥ OptimizeError {
    si nomen.longitudo() ≡ 0 {
        iace finge NomenInane { causa = "empty state name" }
    }
    si possessor.longitudo() ≡ 0 {
        iace finge NomenInane { causa = "empty state owner" }
    }
    si _habeat_solidum(possessor) aut _habeat_solidum(nomen) {
        iace finge NomenInane { causa = "reserved wire character in name or owner" }
    }
    si versio < 1 {
        iace finge VersioInvalida { causa = "invalid state version" }
    }
    si generatio < 1 {
        iace finge GeneratioInvalida { causa = "invalid generation" }
    }
    si passus < 0 {
        iace finge PassusInvalida { causa = "invalid step count" }
    }
    si non (dtype.finita(lentus)) {
        iace finge LentusInvalida { causa = "invalid learning rate" }
    }
    si lentus < 0.0 {
        iace finge LentusInvalida { causa = "invalid learning rate" }
    }
    redde SgdStatum { possessor = possessor, nomen = nomen, versio = versio, generatio = generatio, passus = passus, lentus = lentus }
}

# Public constructor: a fresh state slot for a parameter at generation
# (its current versio), with the per-parameter learning rate. versio = 1,
# passus = 0.
functio structa(textus nomen, textus possessor, numerus generatio, f32 lentus) → SgdStatum ⇥ OptimizeError {
    redde _structum(nomen, possessor, 1, generatio, 0, lentus)
}

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sgd — the optimizer: per-parameter state slots. Uniqueness by
# (possessor, nomen), fail-closed resolution.
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------

genus Sgd {
    lista<SgdStatum> statia

    # Registered state-slot count (one per optimized parameter).
    functio numerus() → numerus {
        redde ego.statia.longitudo()
    }

    # Identity membership by (possessor, nomen).
    functio contineo(textus possessor, textus nomen) → bivalens {
        itera ex ego.statia fixum s {
            si s.possessor() ≡ possessor et s.nomen() ≡ nomen ergo redde verum
        }
        redde falsum
    }

    # Identity resolution — fail closed on a miss.
    functio inveni(textus possessor, textus nomen) → SgdStatum ⇥ OptimizeError {
        itera ex ego.statia fixum s {
            si s.possessor() ≡ possessor et s.nomen() ≡ nomen ergo redde s
        }
        iace finge NomenIgnotum { causa = "no optimizer state for that parameter" }
    }
}

# Field-wise optimizer equality — the whole-checkpoint round-trip
# predicate (same slots, exact field-wise).
functio sgd_aequus(Sgd a, Sgd b) → bivalens {
    si a.numerus() ≠ b.numerus() ergo redde falsum
    itera ex a.statia fixum s {
        fac {
            fixum SgdStatum t ← b.inveni(s.possessor(), s.nomen())
            si non (statum_aequus(s, t)) ergo redde falsum
        }
        cape err {
            redde falsum
        }
    }
    redde verum
}

# Empty optimizer (no state slots).
functio sgd_vacuum() → Sgd {
    redde Sgd { statia = vacua }
}

# Register a state slot. Rejects a duplicate (possessor, nomen) identity.
functio adscisco(Sgd o, SgdStatum s) → Sgd ⇥ OptimizeError {
    si o.contineo(s.possessor(), s.nomen()) {
        iace finge NomenDuplicatum { causa = "optimizer state already registered for that parameter" }
    }
    varia lista<SgdStatum> nova ← o.statia
    nova.appende(s)
    redde Sgd { statia = nova }
}

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Passus — one SGD step's result: the updated parameter and the advanced
# state slot.
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------

genus Passus {
    parametrum.Parametrum novus
    SgdStatum statum

    # The updated parameter (versio bumped by muta).
    functio novus() → parametrum.Parametrum {
        redde ego.novus
    }

    # The advanced state slot (versio +1, generatio = new param versio,
    # passus +1).
    functio statum() → SgdStatum {
        redde ego.statum
    }
}

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# passus — the ONE state mutation: apply a fresh per-parameter gradient to
# the parameter (param' = param − lentus·grad) and advance the state slot.
# Preconditions are explicit and fail closed (see the header contract).
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------

functio passus(SgdStatum s, parametrum.Parametrum p, gradient.Gradiente g) → Passus ⇥ OptimizeError {
    si s.possessor() ≠ p.possessor() aut s.nomen() ≠ p.nomen() {
        iace finge IdentitasMismatch { causa = "state identity does not match the parameter" }
    }
    si g.possessor() ≠ p.possessor() aut g.nomen() ≠ p.nomen() {
        iace finge IdentitasMismatch { causa = "gradient identity does not match the parameter" }
    }
    si gradient.obsoletus(g, p.versio()) {
        iace finge GradusObsoletus { causa = "stale gradient: parameter mutated since the gradient was computed" }
    }
    si parametrum.est_gelida(p) {
        iace finge Gelida { causa = "frozen parameter cannot be optimized" }
    }
    si non (g.valor().figura() ≡ p.figura()) {
        iace finge FormaMismatch { causa = "gradient shape does not match the parameter" }
    }
    fixum lista<f32> datos_p ← p.valor().datos
    fixum lista<f32> datos_g ← g.valor().datos
    varia lista<f32> novus_datos ← vacua
    itera ab 0‥datos_p.longitudo() fixum i {
        fixum f32 pv ← datos_p.accipe(i) vel (0.0 ∷ f32)
        fixum f32 gv ← datos_g.accipe(i) vel (0.0 ∷ f32)
        novus_datos.appende(pv - s.lentus() * gv)
    }
    varia parametrum.Parametrum p2
    fac {
        p2 ← parametrum.muta(p, novus_datos)
    }
    cape err {
        iace finge Mutatio { causa = parametrum.causa(err) }
    }
    redde Passus {
        novus = p2,
        statum = SgdStatum {
            possessor = s.possessor(),
            nomen = s.nomen(),
            versio = s.versio() + 1,
            generatio = p2.versio(),
            passus = s.passus() + 1,
            lentus = s.lentus()
        }
    }
}

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Serialization — versioned wire forms, exact round-trip.
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------

functio serializa_statum(SgdStatum s) → textus {
    varia textus out ← "optimizer/sgd-state/" + schema_versio + "/" + s.possessor() + "/" + s.nomen() + "/" + (s.versio() ↦ textus) + "/" + (s.generatio() ↦ textus) + "/" + (s.passus() ↦ textus) + "/" + (s.lentus() ↦ textus)
    redde out
}

functio deserializa_statum(textus wire) → SgdStatum ⇥ OptimizeError {
    fixum lista<textus> partes ← wire.divide("/")
    si partes.longitudo() ≠ 9 {
        iace finge WireMala { causa = "malformed sgd-state wire" }
    }
    si partes.accipe(0) vel "" ≠ "optimizer" {
        iace finge WireMala { causa = "unknown optimizer marker" }
    }
    si partes.accipe(1) vel "" ≠ "sgd-state" {
        iace finge WireMala { causa = "unknown optimizer-state marker" }
    }
    si partes.accipe(2) vel "" ≠ schema_versio {
        iace finge VersioIgnota { causa = "unknown optimizer schema version" }
    }
    fixum textus possessor ← partes.accipe(3) vel ""
    fixum textus nomen ← partes.accipe(4) vel ""
    fixum textus versio_textus ← partes.accipe(5) vel ""
    fixum textus generatio_textus ← partes.accipe(6) vel ""
    fixum textus passus_textus ← partes.accipe(7) vel ""
    fixum textus lentus_textus ← partes.accipe(8) vel ""
    varia numerus versio ← 0
    varia numerus generatio ← 0
    varia numerus passus ← 0
    varia f32 lentus ← (0.0 ∷ f32)
    si non (_numerica(versio_textus)) {
        iace finge WireMala { causa = "malformed state version in optimizer wire" }
    }
    fac {
        versio ← versio_textus ↦ numerus
    }
    cape err {
        iace finge WireMala { causa = "malformed state version in optimizer wire" }
    }
    si non (_numerica(generatio_textus)) {
        iace finge WireMala { causa = "malformed generation in optimizer wire" }
    }
    fac {
        generatio ← generatio_textus ↦ numerus
    }
    cape err {
        iace finge WireMala { causa = "malformed generation in optimizer wire" }
    }
    si non (_numerica(passus_textus)) {
        iace finge WireMala { causa = "malformed step count in optimizer wire" }
    }
    fac {
        passus ← passus_textus ↦ numerus
    }
    cape err {
        iace finge WireMala { causa = "malformed step count in optimizer wire" }
    }
    fac {
        lentus ← lentus_textus ↦ f32
    }
    cape err {
        iace finge WireMala { causa = "malformed learning rate in optimizer wire" }
    }
    redde _structum(nomen, possessor, versio, generatio, passus, lentus)
}

# The whole-optimizer (checkpoint) wire: count-prefixed, ';'-separated
# slots. The empty optimizer is "optimizer/sgd/1.0.0/0" (no slots).
functio serializa(Sgd o) → textus {
    varia textus out ← "optimizer/sgd/" + schema_versio + "/" + (o.numerus() ↦ textus)
    itera ex o.statia fixum s {
        out ← out + ";" + serializa_statum(s)
    }
    redde out
}

functio deserializa(textus wire) → Sgd ⇥ OptimizeError {
    fixum lista<textus> partes ← wire.divide(";")
    si partes.longitudo() < 1 {
        iace finge WireMala { causa = "malformed optimizer wire" }
    }
    fixum lista<textus> caput ← (partes.accipe(0) vel "").divide("/")
    si caput.longitudo() ≠ 4 {
        iace finge WireMala { causa = "malformed optimizer wire header" }
    }
    si caput.accipe(0) vel "" ≠ "optimizer" {
        iace finge WireMala { causa = "unknown optimizer marker" }
    }
    si caput.accipe(1) vel "" ≠ "sgd" {
        iace finge WireMala { causa = "unknown optimizer marker" }
    }
    si caput.accipe(2) vel "" ≠ schema_versio {
        iace finge VersioIgnota { causa = "unknown optimizer schema version" }
    }
    fixum textus count_textus ← caput.accipe(3) vel ""
    si non (_numerica(count_textus)) {
        iace finge WireMala { causa = "malformed slot count in optimizer wire" }
    }
    varia numerus count ← 0
    fac {
        count ← count_textus ↦ numerus
    }
    cape err {
        iace finge WireMala { causa = "malformed slot count in optimizer wire" }
    }
    si count ≠ partes.longitudo() - 1 {
        iace finge WireMala { causa = "slot count mismatch in optimizer wire" }
    }
    varia lista<SgdStatum> statia ← vacua
    varia numerus i ← 1
    dum i < partes.longitudo() {
        fixum SgdStatum s ← deserializa_statum(partes.accipe(i) vel "")
        statia.appende(s)
        i ← i + 1
    }
    redde Sgd { statia = statia }
}
